<title>USA: Raytheon unit wins $111 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Raytheon unit wins $111 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co said Monday its Savi Technology Inc subsidiary received a $111 million contract to supply radio frequency identification equipment, software and services to the U.S. military.</p>
<p>Assuming all options are exercised, the contract is for five years.</p>
<p>The company said Savi will provide automated radio frequency tags to help the military track the status of goods and supplies.</p>
